    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/senior-officer-research-infrastructure-partnerships-and-operations-in-campbelltown-au-jid-582": {
      "title": "Senior Officer, Research Infrastructure Partnerships and Operations",
      "description": "Senior Officer, Research Infrastructure Partnerships and Operations Division Provost __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Campbelltown, AU Contract Type Casual Job ID: REF1938S Apply Shortlist Casual, short-term appointment at HEW Level 8, up to 35 hours per week. Campbelltown campus with work at Campbelltown Hospital as required. Casual hourly rate: $82.72 to $91.82, plus Superannuation. Lead Faculty planning and operations for a new shared research building. The Opportunity You will lead the Faculty of Health’s involvement in establishing and operationalising a new research building shared across research partners. As the Faculty’s key liaison, you will coordinate its requirements and contributions through planning, commissioning, transition and ongoing operations. You will develop operational plans, processes and service arrangements covering access, onboarding, space, shared equipment and facility use. Working with researchers, partner organisations, University service areas, project teams and facility operators, you will maintain clear communication and progress agreed actions across organisational boundaries. You will support established governance committees by preparing advice, briefings, reports, recommendations and risk information. You will also coordinate the transition to business-as-usual operations, resolve complex operational issues and monitor readiness, performance and emerging requirements to support safe, effective and sustainable research activity. The successful candidate will work from the Lang Walker Medical Research Building (Campbelltown Hospital) and Campbelltown campus, as required. This is a two-month appointment. What Success Looks Like: Faculty requirements are clearly identified and progressed through building planning, commissioning and operational readiness. Practical arrangements are established for access, onboarding, shared equipment, space coordination and facility use. Governance decisions are translated into coordinated Faculty actions, supported by timely advice, reporting and risk information. People, systems, services, documentation and responsibilities are integrated for an effective transition to ongoing operations. Operational risks and stakeholder issues are resolved through evidence-based recommendations and appropriate escalation. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A relevant tertiary qualification, with postgraduate study and extensive relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Extensive experience coordinating research infrastructure, facilities, major projects, research operations or shared services involving multiple stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to develop and implement operational plans, processes and service arrangements within a complex organisation. Highly developed stakeholder engagement, negotiation and liaison skills across partner organisations, disciplines and professional groups. Strong analytical judgement, communication skills and knowledge of safety, risk, compliance and quality requirements in complex research, health or facility settings. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Iona Reid, Faculty General Manager, Health via I.Reid@westernsydney.edu.au. Please include the job reference code REF1938S . Closing Date: 11:59pm, Sunday 18 October 2026. Working Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available. You must provide evidence of your working rights in Australia for the full term of the appointment at time of application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, IT Service Management - Digital Services Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead enterprise IT servi Reference 77653bd1-243b-49da-bb96-0a480288384a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Remuneration & Benefits Specialist Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury and Parramatta South campus