    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/strategic-project-coordinator-in-parramatta-au-jid-581": {
      "title": "Strategic Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Strategic Project Coordinator Division Operations __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1873A Apply Shortlist Full-time, ongoing position Based at Western’s Parramatta South campus Salary: HEW Level 7 $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Shape and implement strategies that strengthen data-informed decisions Develop and implement data, analytics and AI strategies through strong governance, planning and stakeholder engagement. The Opportunity We are seeking an experienced Strategic Project Coordinator to work within the Data Office, supporting the development and implementation of strategies that advance the University’s ability to effectively leverage its data and information assets. Working closely with the Chief Data Officer, you will play a key role in shaping the design and delivery of Western's Data and Analytics Strategy, Roadmap and Operating Model to deliver value to key stakeholders and to leverage data as a strategic asset, while ensuring it is managed and used responsibly. You will translate strategic and operational objectives into expertly crafted documentation, including practical strategies, delivery plans, resource and capacity plans and operating models that strengthen organisational capability and deliver measurable results. You will develop exceptional high-quality documentation, including strategies, plans, schedules, governance briefings, status reports, benefits realisation frameworks, and executive presentations. You will articulate a compelling narrative in these documents which provide clarity and evidence to enable strong oversight and which engender confidence and trust. You will analyse complex information, identify emerging issues and provide practical recommendations that support organisational adoption, informed decision-making and continuous improvement. What Success Looks Like: Success in this role will be demonstrated through the effective development, implementation and coordination of strategic data, analytics and AI priorities. This includes: Strategic roadmaps, plans and initiatives are translated into coordinated implementation activities and delivered within agreed timeframes. Leaders receive clear, accurate and timely governance documentation, analysis and reporting to support decision-making. Milestones, risks, dependencies, deliverables and benefits are actively monitored across concurrent initiatives. Stakeholders are engaged and aligned through effective workshops, consultations and governance forums. Strategic and project activities comply with information governance, privacy, records management and risk obligations. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You The successful candidate will bring experience developing and implementing strategies and coordinating complex initiatives in a large, multifaceted organisation. You will bring: A relevant degree in business, project management, information management, data analytics, organisational development or a related discipline, or equivalent professional experience. Demonstrated experience supporting strategy development and implementation, complex projects, programs or strategic initiatives. Strong planning and organisational capability, with the ability to coordinate concurrent activities, stakeholders and competing priorities. Well-developed stakeholder engagement, relationship management and communication skills, including the ability to present complex information clearly. Sound knowledge of project management principles, governance frameworks and continuous improvement methods, supported by advanced Microsoft 365 skills. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Omer Yezdani, Chief Data Officer via O.Yezdani@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1873A in your email. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Thursday 22nd October 2026, Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortli