    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/lecturer-speech-pathology-in-campbelltown-au-jid-591": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Speech Pathology",
      "description": "Lecturer, Speech Pathology Division Provost __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Campbelltown, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1857P Apply Shortlist Full-time, Fixed-Term position for 2 Years. Based at Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: Academic Level B $125,177 – $147,810 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. NSW Employee Working with Children Check required. Advance speech pathology education through research-informed teaching, curriculum design and student supervision. The Opportunity We are seeking a Lecturer in Speech Pathology to join the School of Health Sciences, contributing to teaching, curriculum development, research and student supervision across speech pathology and related disciplines. You will coordinate, design, deliver and evaluate subjects, incorporating effective assessment, constructive feedback and current research. You will collaborate with academic colleagues to deliver undergraduate education and support students progressing towards postgraduate research and study. You will also undertake research and scholarship, supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research students, and contribute to publications and grant proposals. Through relationships across the School, Faculty, University and external sector, you will support student success and strengthen the discipline’s academic and professional connections. What Success Looks Like: Coordinate and deliver high-quality, research-informed teaching and assessment. Contribute to curriculum and program development in speech pathology. Support undergraduate and postgraduate students to achieve academic success. Produce quality research outputs and contribute to competitive grant proposals. Build productive collaborations across the University and with external partners. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You The successful candidate will bring a strong background in speech pathology, with experience in tertiary teaching and an interest in contributing to research and professional collaboration. You will bring: A doctoral or research master’s qualification relevant to speech pathology, preferably a PhD, or progress towards completing a PhD. A recognised speech pathology qualification and eligibility for Certified Practising membership with Speech Pathology Australia. Experience delivering high-quality teaching and learning in a tertiary environment. Strong relationship-building skills across academic, industry, professional and institutional settings. Research or scholarly experience through publications, presentations, supervision, grant proposals or contributions to research projects. Working with Children Check It is a mandatory requirement for any incumbent of this position to have a current NSW Employee Working with Children Clearance in accordance with the NSW Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Professor Alison Purcell, Head of Discipline, Speech Pathology via A.Purcell@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1857P . Closing Date: 11:59pm, Wednesday 4 November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . As per Part D of the Recruitment and Selection Policy, WSU employees seeking to undertake the position as a secondment must have completed a minimum of 12 months’ full-time continuous service (or equivalent). WSU Employees are encouraged to discuss their interest in a secondment with their current supervisor prior to submitting an application. Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Business Administration Trainee (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Penrith, AU Division Indigenous Leadership Brand Western Sydney University Location Penrith Business Unit Office of the DVC, Indigenous Leadership (U72A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference 4ca10447-80d0-4275-943b-b387118539b7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Business Administration Trainee (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Indigenous Leadership Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Office of the DVC, Indigenous Leadership (U72A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference ae3776d2-867e-41ea-a594-f824e179308b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Business Administration Trainee (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Indigenous Leadership Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Office of the DVC, Indigenous Leadership (U72A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference 0b38ad18-b844-44c1-bf76-7f6980e37271 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Business Administration Trainee (Indigenous Identified Role) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Indigenous Leadership Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the DVC, Indigenous Leadership (U72A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description This is an identified position and applicants must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander Person. Being an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is a genuine occupational qualificati Reference 439aa37b-e6f1-42b8-976d-39361590d163 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Livestock Coordinator Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Property & Commercial (U76F) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position Based at Western’s Hawkesbury (Richmond) campus Salary: HEW Level 5 $87,065 – $98,462 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Manage livestock, pasture and farm operations Reference f423002a-21dd-409f-aedd-cae70054b1df Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Associate Research Fellow - Women's Sexual and Reproductive Health Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Translational Health Research Institute (U73H) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description 2 Years Fixed-Term position at Academic Level A.Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $98,611 – $119,137 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Apply inclusive research Reference bd468cb6-9ec3-4ee8-8c35-c01db9177796 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Remuneration & Benefits Specialist Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury and Parramatta South campuses with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead remuner Reference 0ac8e10e-d401-4a3e-9b53-fc5fc92fbefe Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, IT Service Management - Digital Services Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead enterprise IT servi Reference 77653bd1-243b-49da-bb96-0a480288384a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Apply"
