    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/technical-officer-mass-spectrometry-in-campbelltown-au-jid-604": {
      "title": "Technical Officer, Mass Spectrometry",
      "description": "Technical Officer, Mass Spectrometry Division Research and Innovation (U79) __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Campbelltown, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1885G Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 5. Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $87,065 – $98,462 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Provide technical support, training and instrument expertise for researchers using the Mass Spectrometry Research Facility. The Opportunity You will provide advanced technical support, training and laboratory services within the Mass Spectrometry Research Facility. Your work will support multidisciplinary research by maintaining reliable analytical services, managing sample analysis and helping researchers use specialised instrumentation safely and effectively. You will operate, calibrate and maintain complex analytical equipment, including mass spectrometry systems. You will contribute to analytical method development, laboratory preparation, instrument troubleshooting and the delivery of research projects for internal and external users. You will also maintain laboratory records, chemical inventories, Safety Data Sheets and Standard Operating Procedures. Working with academic staff, students, technical teams, suppliers and research partners, you will help manage competing priorities while maintaining safety, regulatory compliance and operational continuity. What Success Looks Like: Deliver reliable technical support, training and analytical services to researchers and students. Operate, calibrate, troubleshoot and maintain complex laboratory instrumentation. Maintain current laboratory procedures, safety records and chemical inventories. Support research throughput through effective laboratory preparation and sample analysis. Identify and contribute to improvements in technical operations and analytical workflows. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You An undergraduate qualification in Analytical Chemistry, Chemistry, Biochemistry or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Demonstrated experience working in a chemistry laboratory or closely related facility. Experience providing technical support and instruction within laboratory or other specialised practical environments. Strong organisational and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Experience using and maintaining analytical chemistry or mass spectrometry equipment is highly regarded. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Rishi Pandey, Facility Research Manager - Next Generation Sequencing via r.pandey@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1885G. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Friday 30 October 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of your fulltime working rights in Australia for the full term of the appointment at time of application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position Reference 7c5bc823-586d-469d-ba01-f2d83b8712f3 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Future Students Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HYEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead domestic student recruit Reference 2cacbbca-4e61-4fbb-b2fe-b91262703be7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Paid Media Manager Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus