    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/senior-lecturer-medicine-oncology-in-liverpool-au-jid-600": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer Medicine (Oncology)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer Medicine (Oncology) Division Provost __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Liverpool, AU Contract Type Part-Time Job ID: REF1977W Apply Shortlist Part-time 14 hours per week (0.4 FTE), Ongoing position. Based at Liverpool Clinical School. Salary: Academic Level C $60,933.20 – $69,991.20 per annum, plus 17% Super & Leave Loading ( pro-rata based on 0.4 FTE ) . Lead oncology teaching, research and higher degree supervision for medical students while strengthening clinical academic practice. The Opportunity The School of Medicine within the Faculty of Health is seeking to appoint a Senior Lecturer in Oncology in Medicine based at Liverpool Clinical School on a part-time basis. Working within an integrated academic and clinical environment, you will help educate future medical practitioners and advance teaching, research and clinical practice in oncology. You will design and deliver teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate medicine programs, contribute to curriculum development, assessment and feedback, and support student progression and graduate employability. The successful applicant may also hold an associated clinical role within a medicine department in the South Western Sydney Local Health District (SWSLHD), principally at Liverpool Hospital, delivering specialist oncology services alongside their academic responsibilities. What Success Looks Like: Success in this role will be demonstrated through high-quality medical education, research and clinical engagement that advance student learning and the discipline of oncology. This includes: Delivering high-quality, engaging teaching and assessment across undergraduate and postgraduate medicine programs. Developing and delivering oncology teaching for Year 3 students, while contributing to the Year 2 oncology curriculum and teaching program. Supporting student progression and graduate employability through effective curriculum design, assessment and feedback. Producing research and scholarly outcomes that advance knowledge and practice within the discipline. Contributing to clinical service delivery at partner hospitals and strengthening the integration of oncology teaching, research and clinical practice. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You You are an enthusiastic and collaborative medical professional with a strong commitment to education, clinical excellence and research. You bring: A doctoral qualification or equivalent accreditation and standing, with candidates working towards a PhD also considered. Current registration, or eligibility for registration, with the Medical Board of Australia. Specialist training and consultant-level experience in Medical Oncology or Radiation Oncology. A strong track record of high-quality, high-impact research, with the capacity to contribute to research leadership and attract competitive funding. Demonstrated experience in tertiary teaching, curriculum development and educational technologies, with a passion for creating engaging learning experiences and supporting students from diverse backgrounds. A collaborative approach, with the ability to build effective relationships across disciplines, the profession and industry. Experience supervising high-calibre students and contributing to their academic and research development. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Dr Scott MacKenzie, Clinical Dean, Liverpool Clinical School via S.Mackenzie@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1977W . Closing Date: 11:59pm, Thursday 29 October 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position Reference 7c5bc823-586d-469d-ba01-f2d83b8712f3 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Future Students Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing posi