    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/academic-skills-advisor-in-parramatta-au-jid-597": {
      "title": "Academic Skills Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Skills Advisor Division Education & Students __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1992P Apply Shortlist Full-time, 2 Years Fixed-Term positions at HEW Level 7. Penrith, Campbelltown, Bankstown & Parramatta South campuses. Salary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Support student success through inclusive learning services and curriculum-embedded academic skills development. The Opportunity At Western Sydney University Library, we are committed to empowering student success through innovative, inclusive and evidence-informed learning support. Working in partnership with students, academics and professional staff, the Library delivers services and learning experiences that build academic skills, digital capability, research skills and independent learning. Join our Student Skills and Engagement team and play a key role in helping students develop the skills and confidence they need to succeed at university. You will partner with academic staff across disciplines to identify learning needs, with a particular focus on first-year transition and success, and design engaging, curriculum-embedded learning experiences, workshops and targeted support. You will design, deliver and evaluate inclusive learning support across individual, group, online and curriculum-aligned settings. Covering academic writing, critical thinking, communication, study strategies and AI-enabled learning, your work will help students navigate academic expectations, apply feedback and become independent learners. You will also use student engagement, retention and service data to evaluate impact and continuously improve learning support. What Success Looks Like: Deliver inclusive academic skills services across in-person, online and curriculum-embedded settings. Build productive partnerships with academic staff to embed learning development in subjects, courses and programs. Strengthen students’ academic communication, digital capability, study habits and independent learning strategies. Connect students with relevant learning resources, programs and specialist services through appropriate referrals. Use student engagement, retention and service data to evaluate outcomes and improve learning support. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in Education, Linguistics, English, Learning Development, Academic Skills, Communication or a related discipline. Demonstrated experience designing, delivering and evaluating academic skills workshops and developing effective learning resources for in-person and/or online delivery. Specialist knowledge of academic literacies and learning development, including first-year transition and student learning success. Experience collaborating with academic staff across disciplines to design curriculum-embedded learning support and improve student outcomes. Familiarity with effective teaching strategies for students from diverse socio-cultural and language backgrounds, and the ability and willingness to travel between campuses as required. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Campus Preference: Multiple positions are available at Penrith, Campbelltown, Bankstown and Parramatta South campuses. You will be asked to select your campus preference or preferences when applying. Position Enquiries: Direct to Linda Parker, Associate University Librarian, Student Skills & Engagement, via linda.parker@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1992P. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Thursday 12 November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Please note for internal applicants: All ongoing and fixed term employees seeking to apply for this position as a secondment must have completed a minimum of 12 months’ full-time continuous service to be eligible to apply for this role, as per Part D of the Recruitment and Selection Policy. Employees are encouraged to discuss their interest in the opportunity with their current supervisor prior to submitting an application. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Injury Management Coordinator Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW 8 levelHawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Manage complex injury matters and bu Reference 4cb8749e-0738-4ed5-86fd-666ea7b734c7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position Reference 7c5bc823-586d-469d-ba01-f2d83b8712f3 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Future Students Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HYEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead domestic student recruit Reference 2cacbbca-4e61-4fbb-b2fe-b91262703be7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Paid Media Manager Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead paid media strategy and perfor Reference b4628282-91c8-4cb8-8eba-40038b154ab1 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Technical Support Officer, Anatomy Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Education & Students Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Teaching & Research Technical Services (U75D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing positionBased at Western’s Campbelltown campus, with flexible working arrangementsSalary: HEW Level 6 $99,159 – $106,284 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave LoadingCurrent Hepatitis Reference e76c05b0-8060-4ad0-84e5-d1b1b270987f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Technical Officer, Mass Spectrometry Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Research and Innovation (U79) Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Deputy Vice-Chancellor, Research & Innovation (U79A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 5.Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $87,065 – $98,462 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Provide technical support, train Reference afd84a12-0c4d-475c-a00c-238accea9bce Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Restoring Resilient Groundcover Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Hawkesbury Institute for the Environment (U73F) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, 3-Year Fixed-Term position at Academic Level A.Hawkesbury Campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $98,611 – $119,137 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Design field and g Reference faad49f2-efd2-4053-960e-3435859aedc8 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Lecturer Medicine Salary Location Liverpool, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Liverpool Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Academic Description Part-time 7 hours per week (0.2 FTE ), Ongoing position.Based at Liverpool Clinical School.Salary: Academic Level C $30,466.60 – $34,995.60 per annum, plus 17% Super & Leave Loading (pro-rata based on Reference bee2150c-a589-4cc7-b609-b255416829bf Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Marketing & Communications Business Partner Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full time, ongoing position at HEW level 8Hawkesbury and Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangementsSalary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Provide strategi Reference 5fb8628a-daf7-485f-9fcb-d76f09d41c6e Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Apply"
