    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/student-clubs-officer-in-parramatta-au-jid-596": {
      "title": "Student Clubs Officer",
      "description": "Student Clubs Officer Division Education & Students __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1964E Apply Shortlist Appointment: Full-time, Ongoing position Classification: HEW Level 6 (Higher Education Industry General Staff Award) Salary: $85,000 – $95,000 per annum (above award) Location: Western's Parramatta South campus, with flexible working arrangements NSW Employee Working with Children Clearance Required Help shape a thriving student community by empowering clubs and societies, supporting student leaders, and creating opportunities for students to connect, belong and make a lasting impact on campus life. The Opportunity Western Sydney University Student Union is seeking a Student Clubs Officer to work within the Student Engagement team, supporting the growth, sustainability and effective operation of student clubs and societies across Western Sydney University. Working closely with club executives and student leaders, you will provide practical guidance on governance, compliance, funding, events and operational matters. You will coordinate club affiliation and renewal processes, administer funding programs, and support clubs to meet relevant organisational requirements. You will develop and deliver training, resources and communication initiatives that build the capability of club leaders, strengthen membership participation and support inclusive, sustainable club operations. As a key contact for student clubs, you will establish productive relationships with students, staff and stakeholders across diverse communities and interest groups. You will also maintain accurate records, analyse participation, compliance and funding outcomes, and prepare reports and recommendations that support informed decision-making and continuous improvement. This is an exciting opportunity for someone passionate about student engagement and community development to contribute to a vibrant campus culture. Through this work, you will strengthen student leadership, enhance the student experience and foster connection and belonging across the University. This position is classified at HEW Level 6 under the Higher Education Industry General Staff Award . An above-award salary is being offered, with an indicative salary range of $85,000 – $95,000 per annum. What Success Looks Like: Success in this role will be demonstrated through responsive support, sound judgement and effective coordination that enables student clubs to operate sustainably. This includes: Student clubs operating in accordance with governance, compliance, risk and organisational requirements. Club leaders having the knowledge, resources and training required to manage and develop their organisations. Club funding, applications, grants and administrative processes being delivered accurately, efficiently and transparently, supporting positive outcomes for student groups. Productive relationships with student leaders that enable timely and practical support across the clubs network. Increased student participation, leadership opportunities and engagement through relevant programs and initiative. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You The successful candidate will bring relevant program coordination experience, sound judgement and the ability to advise and support diverse student-led groups. You will bring: A relevant degree with experience in community development, education, business, management or student services, or an equivalent combination of relevant education and experience. Demonstrated experience supporting or developing student clubs, community organisations, membership groups, volunteer-led initiatives or student engagement programs. Knowledge of governance, policy compliance, risk assessment and event management within an education, community or not-for-profit environment. Strong organisational and program coordination skills, including the ability to manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes within agreed timeframes. Highly developed communication and stakeholder engagement skills, with the confidence to advise and support a diverse range of student leaders. A passion for student development, leadership and building inclusive communities that foster connection and belonging. Working with Children Check: It is a mandatory requirement for any incumbent of this position to have a current NSW Employee Working with Children Clearance in accordance with the NSW Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Andrew Le, Head of Student Engagement via a.le3@westernsydney.eduau . Please include the job reference code REF1964E in your email. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Sunday 1st November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of your working rights in Australia at time of application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For reasonable adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western Sydney University Student Union Western Sydney University Student Union (WSUSU) is a newly established, student-led not-for-profit organisation dedicated to enhancing student life across Western Sydney University campuses. WSUSU delivers services, programs, advocacy and opportunities that support student wellbeing, engagement, representation and belonging. Working in partnership with students, University stakeholders and the broader community, the Union is focused on building an inclusive, vibrant and student-centred culture across the University’s diverse campus communities. As a growing organisation in its establishment phase, WSUSU offers a unique opportunity to help shape systems, services and experiences that will have a lasting impact on the student community. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Injury Management Coordinator Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW 8 levelHawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Manage complex injury matters and bu Reference 4cb8749e-0738-4ed5-86fd-666ea7b734c7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position Reference 7c5bc823-586d-469d-ba01-f2d83b8712f3 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Future Students Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HYEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead domestic student recruit Reference 2cacbbca-4e61-4fbb-b2fe-b91262703be7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Paid Media Manager Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead paid media strategy and perfor Reference b4628282-91c