    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/support-services-officer-in-parramatta-au-jid-595": {
      "title": "Support Services Officer",
      "description": "Support Services Officer Division Strategy & Planning __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1960J Apply Shortlist Full-time, (35 hours per week), fixed-term parental leave backfill until 10 December 2027 Remuneration: $83,086 p.a. plus Superannuation and Leave Loading Based at Parramatta City Campus (1PSQ) About The College Western Sydney University The College is a not-for-profit wholly owned entity of Western Sydney University. As you consider joining our dynamic team, know that you will be part of an organisation that values growth, inclusivity, and excellence. Learn more about The College here . About the Role Are you highly organised, proactive, and passionate about delivering exceptional administrative support? Join The College as a Support Services Officer and play a key role in ensuring the smooth operation of our directorates and functions. As a Support Services Officer, you’ll play a vital role in ensuring smooth operations and exceptional student experiences. In this dynamic position, you will: Support teaching and business activities across multiple campuses and business units, ensuring smooth day-to-day operations in a dynamic environment. Play a key role in supporting enrolment, attendance and results processes, helping students succeed from start to finish. Support reviews, maintain standards and identify process improvements that make a real difference. Work closely with leadership and cross-functional teams on initiatives that improve services and student engagement. Support diverse higher education operations including those that relate to HR, finance and procurement processes. This is a full-time 35 hours per week, fixed-term parental leave backfill until 10 December 2027 For further information, please refer to the Position Description: Support Services Officer . About You You are a proactive and service-focused administrator who brings: Strong technical skills in Microsoft Office and familiarity with student or learning management systems. Strong administrative experience in a large or complex organisation (tertiary sector desirable). Excellent organisational skills with the ability to balance competing priorities. Clear and confident communication skills, with the ability to support diverse stakeholders. A commitment to accuracy, consistency, and continuous improvement. The ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Why Join us? We offer a supportive and forward-thinking environment where your expertise is valued, and your contributions will make a difference! Joining our team comes with a range of benefits including: 35-hour work week. Remote working options of up to 2 days per week, subject to operational requirements. Generous leave entitlements including 5 weeks of annual leave per year. Professional development – access to leave, grants and training. Additional benefits and more can be found here . Location This position will be based at our Parramatta City Campus (1PSQ), although travel to other campuses of the University may be required. This position is not available in a fully remote format. Remuneration Package: Professional Staff Level 5 $94,450 p.a. (comprising Salary of $83,086 p.a., plus Superannuation and Leave Loading) in accordance with the College Enterprise Agreement. Enquiries: Please direct enquiries about this role to Kit Khamwilai, Manager, Administration Support via email at K.Khamwilai@westernsydney.edu.au Specific enquiries or issues with your application may be directed to the Talent Acquisition Team at talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . Closing date: 11:59pm, Sunday 1 November 2026. Working Rights in Australia - Eligibility You must provide evidence of your full-time working rights in Australia at time of application. Working with Children Check As the College provide education opportunities to ages that include under 18 years olds, it is a prerequisite to have/gain NSW Working with Children Check Clearance. Please note, only those applications submitted via the WSU online recruitment system will be accepted. Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Injury Management Coordinator Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW 8 levelHawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Manage complex injury matters and bu Reference 4cb8749e-0738-4ed5-86fd-666ea7b734c7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position Reference 7c5bc823-586d-469d-ba01-f2d83b8712f3 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortl