    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/senior-manager-support-for-learning-in-parramatta-au-jid-594": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Support for Learning",
      "description": "Senior Manager, Support for Learning Division Education & Students __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1991X Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 9. Parramatta South campus with occasional requirements to work at other sites. $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead the University’s approach to embedded academic skills and learning support, strengthening student capability, engagement and success. The Opportunity Western Sydney University Library empowers student success through inclusive, evidence-informed learning support. Working in partnership with students, academics and professional staff, the Library delivers services, resources and learning experiences that build academic skills, digital capability, research skills and independent learning. In this role, you will set the strategic direction for the University Library’s approach to embedded academic skills and learning support. Leading a team of Learning Partnerships Librarians and Academic Skills Advisors, you will shape scalable, curriculum-embedded approaches that strengthen students’ academic literacies, digital capability, confidence, engagement and academic success. Working closely with academic and professional stakeholders across the University, you will influence institutional practice and build productive curriculum partnerships. You will use student data, learning analytics, evaluation evidence, sector intelligence and emerging technologies to improve the quality, reach and equity of learning support while ensuring services remain aligned with University priorities and the evolving needs of a diverse student community. What Success Looks Like: Deliver sustainable, university-wide approaches to curriculum-embedded academic literacies. Build partnerships that embed academic skills, digital capability, learning resources and independent learning within curricula. Lead workforce planning, capability development and change across a sizeable professional team. Establish service standards, operating models and performance measures across campuses, cohorts and delivery modes. Use data, feedback and evaluation evidence to demonstrate impact and guide continuous improvement. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A postgraduate qualification and professional experience in education, learning development, academic literacies, higher education, library and information studies, or a related discipline. Extensive experience leading learning support, academic skills, learning development or curriculum-embedded services in higher education. Demonstrated people leadership experience, including workforce planning, performance development, capability building and change leadership. Proven ability to influence senior academic and professional stakeholders and build effective curriculum partnerships. Strong strategic thinking and the ability to use complex data and evaluation evidence to guide decisions, allocate resources and improve student outcomes. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Linda Parker, Associate University Librarian, Student Skills & Engagement via Linda.Parker@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1991X. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Thursday 12 November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Injury Management Coordinator Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW 8 levelHawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Manage complex injury matters and bu Reference 4cb8749e-0738-4ed5-86fd-666ea7b734c7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position Reference 7c5bc823-586d-469d-ba01-f2d83b8712f3 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more