    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/technical-support-officer-humanities-education-and-arts-in-parramatta-au-jid-612": {
      "title": "Technical Support Officer, Humanities, Education & Arts",
      "description": "Technical Support Officer, Humanities, Education & Arts Division Education & Students __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Parramatta, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1924S Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position Based at Western’s Parramatta South campus, with a requirement to work at other campuses based on operational needs Salary: HEW Level 5 $87,065 – $98,462 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading Provide adaptable technical support for teaching and research across humanities, education and creative arts disciplines. The Opportunity We are seeking a Technical Support Officer to work within the Humanities, Education & Arts team in Teaching & Research Technical Services. You will support teaching and research across a multidisciplinary portfolio that may include creative arts, photographic and digital media, game development and PDHPE. You will prepare practical teaching spaces, materials and equipment, assist students and staff, and help maintain specialist facilities, software and technologies. You will promote the safe use of laboratories, studios, workshops and other practical environments by completing risk assessments, maintaining safety documentation and supporting the appropriate handling, storage and disposal of hazardous materials. You will also develop and maintain standard operating procedures, contribute to audits and stocktakes, and assist with minor equipment and consumable purchases. This is a generalist role that requires you to adapt to changing teaching timetables, research activities and operational priorities. While primarily based at Parramatta South Campus, you will work flexibly across disciplines, technical environments and University campuses as required. What Success Looks Like: Success in this role will be demonstrated through safe, reliable and responsive technical services that support high-quality teaching and research. This includes: Preparing and maintaining specialist facilities, equipment and materials for practical teaching and research activities. Providing clear technical and safety guidance to students, academic staff and professional staff. Maintaining risk assessments, Safety Data Sheets, chemical inventories and standard operating procedures. Completing audits, stocktakes and corrective actions accurately and within required timeframes. Contributing to continuous process improvement across the Humanities, Education & Arts technical portfolio. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You The successful candidate will bring broad technical capability, sound safety judgement and the adaptability to support multiple disciplines and practical environments. You will bring: An undergraduate degree in humanities, arts or education, or an equivalent combination of relevant education, training and experience. Experience providing technical support in specialist humanities or arts-based facilities and environments. Experience preparing practical teaching spaces such as laboratories, studios and workshops. Well-developed organisational skills, including the ability to prioritise competing tasks and meet deadlines. Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills, digital capability and experience working with chemicals, dangerous goods or biologically hazardous materials. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Jennie Nelson, Technical Manager, Science, Education & Humanities via J.Nelson@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1924S in your email. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Thursday 12th November 2026. Working Rights: You must provide evidence of your working rights in Australia at time of application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For reasonable adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Come and join our team at Hawkesbury campusSalary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into trusted i Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Student Clubs Officer Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Education & Students Brand Western Sydney University Student Union Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the DVC, Education & Students (U75F) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Appointment: Full-time, Ongoing positionClassification: HEW Level 6 (Higher Education Industry General Staff Award)Salary: $85,000 – $95,000 per annum (above award)Location: Western's Parramatta South Reference b8da7f95-02ae-42ae-b359-81e265501859 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor in Surgery Salary Location Parkside Cres, Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Academic Description Part-time, Ongoing position at A