    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/manager-future-student-engagement-in-richmond-au-jid-610": {
      "title": "Manager, Future Student Engagement",
      "description": "Manager, Future Student Engagement Division Western Sydney & External Engagement __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Richmond, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF2019X Apply Shortlist Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 8. Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead domestic student recruitment strategies that improve engagement, conversion and enrolment outcomes across priority cohorts. The Opportunity You will lead the planning, implementation and performance of domestic student recruitment activity across allocated regions, cohorts or recruitment portfolios. Translating University strategy into targeted plans, you will establish clear priorities, timelines and measures that contribute to domestic student enrolment targets. You will use recruitment data, market intelligence and student insights to identify opportunities across school leaver, non-school leaver and postgraduate markets. By monitoring the recruitment pipeline from initial engagement through to enrolment, you will identify performance gaps, implement targeted interventions and recommend where resources and investment will have the greatest impact. You will provide functional leadership to future student engagement staff, managing workloads, capability and operational performance. Working across Marketing, Market Insights and Data, Admissions, Faculties, Student Success and Services, you will build alignment across the recruitment journey and provide strategic advice on performance, market opportunities, risks and continuous improvement. What Success Looks Like: Deliver targeted recruitment plans that contribute to domestic enrolment targets. Improve engagement, lead generation, application, conversion and enrolment outcomes. Use recruitment data and market intelligence to identify gaps and guide interventions. Build strong relationships with schools, education providers, communities and partners. Lead staff, budgets and resources against clear recruitment priorities and measures. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A relevant tertiary qualification and extensive experience in student recruitment, engagement, marketing, business development, education or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience leading domestic student recruitment, engagement or conversion activities that achieved measurable outcomes. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with experience using recruitment data, market intelligence and student insights. People leadership experience encompassing staff development, performance management and workload prioritisation. Highly developed stakeholder engagement, negotiation, influencing and communication skills across complex organisations and external partnerships. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Kellie Burke, Director, Domestic Student Recruitment via kellie.burke@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF2019X Closing Date: 11:59pm, Wednesday 11th November 2026 Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Workforce Reporting Analyst Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 7.Come and join our team at Hawkesbury campusSalary: $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Turn complex workforce data into trusted i Reference 50d75530-607d-459c-b411-013e1c3ca41c Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Student Clubs Officer Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Education & Students Brand Western Sydney University Student Union Location Parramatta Business Unit Office of the DVC, Education & Students (U75F) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Appointment: Full-time, Ongoing positionClassification: HEW Level 6 (Higher Education Industry General Staff Award)Salary: $85,000 – $95,000 per annum (above award)Location: Western's Parramatta South Reference b8da7f95-02ae-42ae-b359-81e265501859 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor in Surgery Salary Location Parkside Cres, Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Academic Description Part-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level C or D.Macarthur Clinical School location.Salary: Level C $152,333 – $174,978 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading (Pro-rata). Level D $182,520 – Reference b61a3114-6e3c-4677-ae51-310555bda346 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Lecturer/ Associate Professor, Critical Care Salary Location Parkside Cres, Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Part-Time Position Category Academic Description 0.2 FTE Part-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level C or D.Macarthur Clinical School.Salary: Level C $152,333 – $174,978 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading (Pro-rata). Level D $182,520 – Reference 054875d6-1514-4b91-8e4e-98ddb339f48d Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Marketing Manager, Product and Domestic Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus (with requirements to also travel to Parramatta and Campbelltown) with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, Reference b4b4c3e6-068f-4685-82f1-f25b09c600cf Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Technical Support Officer, Humanities, Education & Arts Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Education & Students Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Teaching & Research Technical Services (U75D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position Based at Western’s Parramatta South campus, with a requirement to work at other campuses based on operational needsSalary: HEW Level 5 $87,065 – $98,462 per annum, plus 17% Reference 27cc07c4-e02e-49de-a2a1-4aa83eff0421 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Future Students Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead domestic student recruitm Reference 2cacbbca-4e61-4fbb-b2fe-b91262703be7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Anatomy Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Teach medical sciences, d Reference 516d1455-dee7-4d5e-9056-6ed7e1c1ca4a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Injury Management Coordinator Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW 8 levelHawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Manage complex injury matters and bu Reference 4cb8749e-0738-4ed5-86fd-666ea7b734c7 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Head of Indigenous Future Students Engagement Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Western Sydney & External Engagement Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Future Students, Marketing and Communications (U77A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Hawkesbury campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. This is an identified position Reference 7c5bc823-586d-469d-ba01-f2d83b8712f3 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Apply"
